an pedigree is evident in its use of blue notes, call-and-response, improvisation, polyrhythms, syncopation, and the swung note of ragtime.\n\nFrom its early development until the present, jazz has also incorporated music from 19th and 20th century American popular music, which is based on European music traditions.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Lady Gaga", "streams": 46239, "best_position": 20}, {"artist": "Kendrick Lamar", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Laufey", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Rex Orange County", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Sienna Spiro", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Steve Lacy", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "my", "country_name": "Malaysia", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "KATSEYE", "streams": 27647, "best_position": 57}, {"artist": "CORTIS", "streams": 25808, "best_position": 72}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": 25613, "best_position": 76}, {"artist": "ENHYPEN", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Hearts2Hearts", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "IVE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Jennie", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist"